  "raw": {
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUSA_External/job/San-Antonio-TX/Associate-Professor-of-Communication-and-Student-Media-Director_R-097951-1": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Communication and Student Media Director",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nJob Title Associate Professor of Communication and Student Media Director Agency Texas A&M University - San Antonio Department Department of Sociology and Communication Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location San Antonio, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Sociology and Communication at Texas A&M University-San Antonio invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Associate Professor of Communication and Student Media Director, beginning in Fall 2027. This position combines faculty responsibilities with leadership of the University's award-winning Jaguar Student Media Network (JSMN), a comprehensive student media enterprise that serves as a cornerstone of experiential learning in the Communication Program. The successful candidate will teach three undergraduate courses annually (2/1 teaching load) and provide strategic vision, administration, and mentorship for the University's student media operations. We seek an accomplished teacher-scholar and media leader with expertise in journalism, digital media, media production, multimedia storytelling, strategic communication, sports media, broadcasting, or a related field. Candidates should demonstrate a record of excellence in teaching, scholarship, creative activity, and/or professional practice appropriate for appointment at the rank of associate professor. The successful candidate will be committed to student-centered learning, workforce preparation, and advancing opportunities for experiential and community-engaged education. About the Jaguar Student Media Network Established in 2010, the Jaguar Student Media Network provides engaging public forums that inform, educate, and connect students, faculty, staff, and the broader South Texas community. Through state-of-the-art communication laboratories and student-led media operations, JSMN reaches thousands of readers, viewers, and listeners annually through original reporting, storytelling, entertainment, and multimedia content. As part of Texas A&M University-San Antonio's mission as a Hispanic-Serving Institution, the Jaguar Student Media Network is dedicated to preparing the next generation of Latino media and communication professionals. The Network serves as an extension of the University's commitment to empowering students through innovative academic and co-curricular experiences that foster leadership, civic engagement, and career readiness. The Jaguar Student Media Network consists of three integrated student media operations: The Mesquite Online News A student-run hyper-local digital news organization that provides hands-on training in reporting, writing, editing, multimedia storytelling, data journalism, and community-focused journalism. Students produce original coverage of campus, community, and regional issues while developing professional journalism skills. El Espejo Magazine A student-produced magazine that offers opportunities for creative storytelling, feature writing, photography, visual design, and multimedia content creation. El Espejo showcases student voices and perspectives through innovative and culturally relevant content. Enlace Media Lab A multimedia production and broadcast hub that provides students with opportunities to create digital entertainment and media content across multiple platforms. Enlace includes Jaguar Radio and the emerging Jaguar Sports Network, offering experiential training in broadcasting, podcasting, live production, sports media, audio storytelling, video production, and content creation. University and Program Profile Texas A&M University–San Antonio is part of the internationally recognized Texas A&M University System. Established as a stand-alone university in 2009, A&M– San Antonio is a comprehensive four-year public university that reflects the culturally and historically rich community it serves. Located on nearly 700 acres in South San Antonio, the University offers 37 undergraduate degree programs and 19 graduate degree programs to more than A&M–San Antonio is designated as a Hispanic-Serving Institution and is one of only 30 higher education institutions in the United States to have earned the Seal of Excelencia certification from Excelencia in Education in recognition of its commitment to Latino student success. More than 77% of A&M–San Antonio students identify as Latinx, 66% identify as women, and approximately 60% are the first in their families to attend college. These students bring a wealth of cultural knowledge, professional experience, and community connections to the classroom, creating meaningful opportunities for faculty committed to teaching, mentorship, and publicly engaged scholarship. In December 2022, the University established a partnership with the Texas A&M University Health Science Center, also known as Texas A&M Health, and University Health, the Bexar County public health system. This affiliation brings together three nationally recognized institutions to develop and expand educational pathways and research opportunities in high-demand health sciences fields, particularly within a historically underserved region. Part of the Department of Sociology and Communication, the Communication Program offers a Bachelor of Arts in Communication with concentrations in Mass Communication and Media. The program combines the study of communication theory, research, media processes, and professional practice to prepare students to become ethical, effective communicators. Through a flexible and interdisciplinary curriculum, students develop critical thinking, media literacy, storytelling, and collaborative problem-solving skills that support careers in media, journalism, digital content creation, and related communication professions. Our communication students annually earn regional and national distinction, competing for and winning awards, scholarships, grants, and professional development opportunities. Since the launch of the academic program in 2010, our students have received scholarships from the National Association of Hispanic Journalists (NAHJ), Google, the Online News Association (ONA), the Society of Professional Journalists (SPJ), the San Antonio Association of Hispanic Journalists (SAAHJ), the San Antonio Professional Chapter of Women in Communications, as well as awards from the Texas Intercollegiate Press Association (TIPA), the Mark of Excellence Awards from the Society of Professional Journalists (SPJ), an Emmy from the National Academy of Television Arts & Sciences, and admission to the Boston University Graduate College of Communication, and the UC Berkeley Graduate School of Journalism among others. Job Responsibilities: Faculty Responsibilities Teach the equivalent of 9 course credits per academic year (2/1 teaching load) in Communication including internship and media courses. Develop a research program at A&M-SA that results in tangible products (articles, books, grants, etc.). As part of an involved Communication Program team, provide service at the program, department, college, university, community, and profession levels. Media Director Responsibilities Leadership & Oversight: Provide leadership direction to multiple student media outlets (e.g., Digital News, Print Magazine, Internet Radio, Multimedia Production, Jaguar Sports Network, and Jag TV). Ensure that all student media operate within university policies and journalistic ethics. Serve as a liaison between student media and university administration. Operational Management : Oversee budgets, equipment, and facilities for student media. Coordinate fundraising, grant writing, and revenue-generation efforts (sometimes in conjunction with students or university departments). Coordinate Faculty and Student Travel for student contests and media conventions. Ensure timely publication and resourcing to ensure distribution of content (print, broadcast, digital). Strategic Planning & Innovation: Develop long-term strategies for growth, sustainability, and modernization of student media. Encourage digital transformation and integration of new technologies (e.g., podcasts, social media strategy, mobile platforms, and university-wide streaming). Compliance & Risk Management: Ensure student media complies with copyright laws, libel standards, and FCC regulations. Help mitigate legal or reputational risks by reviewing controversial or sensitive content when needed (without infringing editorial independence). Collaboration & Outreach: Build relationships with faculty, departments (e.g., journalism, communications), alumni, and external media organizations. Promote student media work across campus and in the community. Required Education and Experience: A Ph.D. in Communication is required. Outstanding research potential. Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the university level, professional service. Previous experience serving as director of student media or adviser to a student media outlet is required. We will consider hiring someone at the Assistant Professor rank if they are an outstanding candidate. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to complete tasks and work cooperatively with others. Strong self-discipline and ability to work independently. Ability to communicate effectively with faculty, staff, and students. Ability to interact with students from a range of backgrounds. Applicant Instructions:   Please make sure to provide the following documents:  Cover Letter Resume / CV  Overview of research experiences and current research agenda (2 pages or less). Overview of teaching experiences and teaching philosophy (2 pages or less). Overview of experiences advising or directing student media and vision for a contemporary student media program (2 pages or less). Contact information for three references that will provide letters of recommendation, if requested. For detailed instructions on how to apply for any position on our website, please use the following link:  http://www.tamusa.edu/humanresources/job-opportunities/index.html ​   The position is open until filled, but review of applications will begin within one month of posting. If selected for the position, prior to issuing a letter of appointment, the official transcripts must be received directly from each degree-granting institution. We cannot accept transcripts issued directly to the candidate. If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective candidate to have the transcript translated, evaluated and notarized. Verified Electronic Copies of Official transcript should be sent to: joni.foster@tamusa.edu If necessary, hard copies of official transcripts should be sent directly from the issuing institution to the address listed below: Associate Professor of Communication and Student Media Director c/o Joni Foster (e-mail: Joni.Foster@tamusa.edu) Office of the Provost Texas A&M University- San Antonio One University Way San Antonio, Texas 78224 Selected candidate must pass a pre-employment background investigation to be hired for the position. The above duties may not be performed in every position with this title and the above functions may not include all related duties that might be performed. This position requires physical activities supportive of the above job duties. Reasonable accommodations will be made as necessary. Summary of Employee Benefits:   www.tamusa.edu/human-resources/documents/Summary-of-Employees-Benefits1.pdf Texas A&M University-San Antonio values community engagement and encourages applicants who are committed to advancing the well-being and prosperity of our communities.  Please ensure that all required documents are uploaded prior to submitting the application. Once the application is submitted, no changes or revisions can be made.  If you have issues with adding documents to your application, please contact HR at 210-784-2058.   In compliance with ADA, if accommodations are needed for the application process, please contact HR at (210) 784-2058.  A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee. In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status, this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUSA_External/job/San-Antonio-TX/Lecturer_R-097949-1": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nJob Title Lecturer of Mathematics Agency Texas A&M University - San Antonio Department Department of Computational, Engineering, and Mathematical Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location San Antonio, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Computational, Engineering, and Mathematical Sciences at Texas A&M University-San Antonio (A&M-SA) seeks applications from qualified candidates, with a passion for teaching, for a full-time non-tenure-track Lecturer position in mathematics. Appointment can begin in Spring 2027. The specialization is open, but applicants should be qualified to teach both math and statistics courses. Excellence in teaching at all levels of the curriculum, and ability and willingness to collaborate with colleagues on improving success rates in entry-level mathematics courses is expected. Contribution to improving student success in entry level mathematics courses is a high priority for the institution. The base teaching load at A&M-SA for lecturers is 5/5; reassigned time for service is possible. Summer teaching assignments may be available but are not guaranteed. Service to the department, college, university, and the community is dependent on teaching load. This is a position that requires teaching in person on campus, though a few courses may be taught online. The Department provides a rich educational experience for students interested in computing, cybersecurity, engineering technology, and mathematics. We offer bachelor’s degree programs in these disciplines as also support courses in physics for STEM majors. We also offer Master's degree programs in Computer Science and Cybersecurity. Our students enjoy learning in person and in online/hybrid courses with small class sizes, and state-of-the-art technology, in high-tech classrooms. We emphasize hands-on experiential learning and critical thinking, and the participation of students in research under our faculty’s mentorship. A&M-SA is committed to excellence. We recruit faculty that enhance the breadth, depth and quality of our students' educational experiences by providing a variety of role models and mentors for our student population. Such faculty help us attract, retain, and graduate students more successfully. In this context applicants are required to address, in their cover letter, how their life experiences, work history, professional engagement, and relevant community engagements will contribute to the success of our students, and what the applicants' plans are for serving our student population. Salary: Commensurate with experience and qualifications. Required Education and Experience: A Master’s degree in Mathematics or a closely related field from a regionally accredited institution. All areas will be considered. A minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in mathematics. Evidence of potential for improving student success in entry level mathematics courses. Excellent teaching and communication skills. Preferred Education and Experience: Experience in teaching mathematics, commensurate with the rank of Lecturer (teaching advanced topics in High School and/or Graduate Teaching Assistantship count). Experience in collaboration with faculty on projects geared toward students’ academic success. In the cover letter please speak to the following topics: Engagement with teaching Mathematics. Experience with improving student success in entry level Mathematics courses. Evidence-based potential for excellence in mathematics teaching at the university level, commensurate with the rank of Lecturer. Applicant Instructions:   Please make sure to provide the following documents:  Cover Letter Resume / CV  Professional References For detailed instructions on how to apply for any position on our website, please use the following link:  http://www.tamusa.edu/humanresources/job-opportunities/index.html ​   Application review will begin as soon as they are submitted. The position is open until filled. Finalists (and only finalists) must request at least three current letters of recommendation, with the subject ‘Lecturer of Mathematics –Letter of Recommendation – Applicant Name’ to be sent directly by the author via postal mail (Address: Mr. Anthony Hudgins, Department of CEMS, Texas A&M University-San Antonio, One University Way, San Antonio, TX 78224) or by email delivery (ahudgins@tamusa.edu). The letter of recommendation should be written on official letterhead, be less than one year old, and must bear the writer's actual signature. If selected, finalists must pass a pre-employment background investigation to be appointed to the position. Official transcripts of the candidate selected for the position must be on file with the Office of the Provost, and sent directly from each degree-granting institution to Texas A&M University-San Antonio (1) to the address listed below or (2) sent electronically to vuddameri@tamusa.edu. We cannot accept transcripts issued directly to the candidate. If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator (e.g., AACRAO; http://www.aacrao.org/credential/index.htm). Texas A&M University-San Antonio Chair, Department of Computational, Engineering, and Mathematical Sciences Texas A&M University-San Antonio ATTN: Dr. Venki Uddameri One University Way San Antonio, Texas 78224 Please direct any questions to Dr. Venki Uddameri, Chair CEMS Department: (vuddameri@tamusa.edu). Summary of Employee Benefits:   www.tamusa.edu/human-resources/documents/Summary-of-Employees-Benefits1.pdf Texas A&M University-San Antonio values community engagement and encourages applicants who are committed to advancing the well-being and prosperity of our communities.  Please ensure that all required documents are uploaded prior to submitting the application. Once the application is submitted, no changes or revisions can be made.  If you have issues with adding documents to your application, please contact HR at 210-784-2058.   In compliance with ADA, if accommodations are needed for the application process, please contact HR at (210) 784-2058.  A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee. In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status, this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUSA_External/job/San-Antonio-TX/Assistant-Professor-of-Cyber-Engineering-Technology---Computer-Science_R-097145-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Cyber Engineering Technology & Computer Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Professor of Cyber Engineering Technology & Computer Science Agency Texas A&M University - San Antonio Department Department of Computational, Engineering, and Mathematical Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location San Antonio, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Computational, Engineering and Mathematical Sciences invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Cyber Engineering Technology (CET) beginning Spring/Summer 2027. We seek an innovative educator and scholar whose expertise lies at the intersection of electronics, embedded systems, and cybersecurity . The successful candidate will contribute to the continued development of our Cyber Engineering Technology program while fostering strong collaboration with the Department's Electronics Systems Technology (ESET) and Cybersecurity, Computer Science and Mathematics programs as appropriate.  A&M-SA is a fast-growing comprehensive regional university with over 7,500 students. It is part of the statewide Texas A&M University System, A&M-SA is located on 694 acres in south San Antonio and serves a multi-cultural student body, offering academic programs that meet regional needs. The campus, with Mudéjar style buildings and contemporary facilities that leverage technology to enhance the student experience, embraces the spirit of San Antonio’s rich culture. Self-reported demographic data indicate 60% of students are the first generation in their family in college, and 66% women. We seek to recruit faculty that enhance the breadth, depth, and quality of our students' educational experience.   We are committed to the success of first-generation college students and military veterans.   In this context applicants should address, in their cover letter, how their life experiences, work history, professional engagement, and relevant community engagement will contribute to the success of our students, and what the applicants' plans are for serving our student population. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: Hardware and embedded systems security , including secure hardware architectures, firmware, trusted computing, FPGA security, and hardware-assisted cryptography. Internet of Things (IoT) and edge computing security , including embedded devices, wireless communications, industrial IoT, and secure sensing platforms. Cyber-physical systems and critical infrastructure security , including industrial control systems (ICS), operational technology (OT), smart manufacturing, robotics, transportation, water, energy, and other intelligent infrastructure. Applied cybersecurity for electronic systems , including hardware assurance, secure system design, vulnerability analysis, cyber resilience, and AI-enabled cyber defense. Applicants with experience integrating cybersecurity principles into electronics, embedded systems, automation, or intelligent infrastructure are especially encouraged to apply. The Department is committed to preparing graduates who can design, build, secure, and operate modern cyber-enabled engineering systems. The Cyber Engineering Technology program emphasizes applied learning through laboratories, project-based instruction, undergraduate research, industry collaboration, and experiential education.  Faculty are encouraged to pursue interdisciplinary research spanning cybersecurity, engineering, artificial intelligence, robotics, intelligent infrastructure, digital twins, and resilient cyber-physical systems.  Salary: Commensurate with experience and qualifications. Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate courses primarily in cyber engineering technology and electronics systems engineering technology.  Ability to teach undergraduate and graduate level courses in cybersecurity and computer science as appropriate. Contribute to impactful research and mentoring of both undergraduate and graduate students. Contribute to the service mission of the university. Required Education and Experience: An earned Ph.D. or Doctor of Engineering in Cyber-Engineering or a related field by the time of the appointment.  The candidate’s expertise and experience must focus on the security of hardware, IoT, embedded or cyber-physical systems. Candidates with ABD status will be considered if the requirements for the Ph.D. degree are completed before the appointment begins (degree conferral may happen later). A commitment to teaching excellence, especially at the undergraduate level, using hands-on experiential learning methods. Demonstrated potential of scholarly activity with an ability to secure external funding.  Strong written and oral communication skills.  An entrepreneurial mindset with a focus on contributing to department and university growth. Demonstration of excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Education and Experience: Teaching at the university level ( Graduate Teaching Assistant Experience in these areas will also be considered ). Candidates with industrial experience in the hardware aspects of cybersecurity, professional certifications related to cybersecurity and experience developing and teaching laboratory courses using embedded systems, programmable logic controllers and robotics will be given preference.  Applicant Instructions:   Please make sure to provide the following documents:  Cover Letter Resume / CV  Professional References Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research interests Unofficial copies of transcripts For detailed instructions on how to apply for any position on our website, please use the following link:  http://www.tamusa.edu/humanresources/job-opportunities/index.html ​   This position is open until filled. Finalists must request at least three current letters of recommendation, with the subject ‘Assistant Professor of Cyber Engineering Technology – Letter of Recommendation – Applicant Name’ to be sent directly by the author to the Search Committee Chair of Cyber Engineering Technology via postal mail (Address: Department of CEMS, Texas A&M University-San Antonio, One University Way, San Antonio, TX 78224) or by email delivery (ahudgins@tamusa.edu). If selected, finalists must pass a pre-employment background investigation to be appointed to the position. Official transcripts of the candidate selected for the position must be on file with the Office of the Provost and sent directly from each degree-granting institution to Texas A&M University-San Antonio (1) to the address listed below or (2) sent electronically to ahudgins@tamusa.edu. We cannot accept transcripts issued directly to the candidate. If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator (e.g., AACRAO; http://www.aacrao.org/credential/index.htm ). Texas A&M University-San Antonio Search Committee Chair, Cyber Engineering Technology Department of Computational, Engineering, and Mathematical Sciences Texas A&M University-San Antonio One University Way San Antonio, Texas 78224 Summary of Employee Benefits:   www.tamusa.edu/human-resources/documents/Summary-of-Employees-Benefits1.pdf Texas A&M University-San Antonio values community engagement and encourages applicants who are committed to advancing the well-being and prosperity of our communities.  Please direct any questions to the department chair – Venki Uddameri, Ph.D., P.E (vuddameri@tamusa.edu). Please ensure that all required documents are uploaded prior to submitting the application. Once the application is submitted, no changes or revisions can be made.  If you have issues with adding documents to your application, please contact HR at 210-784-2058.   In compliance with ADA, if accommodations are needed for the application process, please contact HR at (210) 784-2058. A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee. In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status, this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUSA_External/job/San-Antonio-TX/Adjunct-Faculty-in-Physics_R-095729": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Physics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-30\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty in Physics Agency Texas A&M University - San Antonio Department Department of Computational, Engineering, and Mathematical Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location San Antonio, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Computational, Engineering and Mathematical Sciences (CEMS), in the College of Arts and Sciences, seeks applications from qualified candidates for a part-time non-tenure track position in Physics. We seek qualified instructors to teach face-to-face lecture and laboratory courses during the daytime hours in introductory College Physics (algebra based) and University Physics (calculus-based) course sequences.  This is for the Fall semester with potential to teach in the Spring 2027 and summer 2027 as well. Responsibilities include creating and maintaining a safe environment for instruction and learning in a laboratory setting. Salary: 3-hour lecture courses = $3000, 3-hour laboratory = $2000 Required Education and Experience: Master’s degree in Physics or a related field, from a regionally accredited institution Must have 18 graduate credit hours in related area. Preferred Education and Experience: Experience teaching at the college level Experience working with all students from different backgrounds and settings Completed Ph.D. in Physics or related field. Required Special Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others. Strong self-discipline and ability to work independently. Strong quantitative and qualitative analytical skills. Application Instructions: For detailed instructions on how to apply for any positions on our website, please use the following link: http://www.tamusa.edu/humanresources/job-opportunities/index.html ​ Applicants must submit the following to be considered:  Application A Curriculum Vitae (CV) A Letter of Interest – make sure to include which introductory Physics courses and labs you feel comfortable teaching and a teaching statement/philosophy. · Contact information for three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Finalists will be required to provide three current, original letters of recommendation to the Search Committee Chair.  The letters should be less than one year old and should bear the writer’s actual signature. Before issuing a letter of appointment, official transcripts (hard copy or verified e-copy) must be received directly from each degree-granting institution.   We cannot accept transcripts issued directly to the candidate. If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator. Verified Electronic Copies of Official transcript should be sent to: e-mail: Tamara.Guillen@tamusa.edu Hard Copies of Official transcripts should be sent to the address listed below: Adjunct Faculty of Physics Position c/o Tamara Guillen Dept. of Computational, Engineering and Mathematical Sciences Texas A&M University- San Antonio One University Way San Antonio, Texas 78224 The selected candidates must pass a pre-employment background investigation to be hired for this position.  Please direct any questions to Venki Uddameri, Ph.D, Chair - Dept. of Computational, Engineering and Mathematical Sciences at vuddameri@tamusa.edu   Summary of Employee Benefits:  https://www.tamusa.edu/human-resources/documents/summary-of-employees-benefits.pdf    Texas A&M University-San Antonio values community engagement and encourages applicants who are committed to advancing the well-being and prosperity of our communities.  Please ensure that all required documents are uploaded before applying. Once the application is submitted, no changes or revisions can be made.  If you have issues with adding documents to your application, please contact HR at 210-784-2058.  In compliance with ADA, if accommodations are needed for the application process, please contact HR at (210) 784-2058.  All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee. In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status, this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUSA_External/job/San-Antonio-TX/Associate-Professor-in-Educational-Leadership--Dissertation-and-Research-_R-091501-1": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor in Educational Leadership (Dissertation and Research)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-23\nFull time\n\nJob Title Associate/Full Professor in Educational Leadership (Dissertation and Research) Agency Texas A&M University - San Antonio Department Department Of Educator & Leadership Preparation Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location San Antonio, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The College of Education and Human Development (COEHD) at Texas A&M University-San Antonio (A&M-SA) invites applications for a tenure track/tenured appointment at the rank of Ass ociate/Full Professor of Education Leadership beginning in Spring 2027 . The Associate/Full Professor of Educational Leadership position includes teaching both graduate and doctoral courses in educational leadership. The successful candidate will be trained in educational leadership. Additionally, a successful candidate will have significant experience chairing dissertations. The candidate must have a demonstrated record of successfully mentoring doctoral candidates through degree completion. Additional responsibilities include teaching the equivalent of between two to three 3 credit hour courses in education leadership during fall and spring semesters. Teaching assignments may include day, night, or weekend classes. Flexible to suit the course schedule. The candidate must be willing to work in a collaborative and fast-paced environment, and be familiar with the needs of a non-traditional, first-generation, multicultural student body. Responsibilities are general in nature and may reflect more than one functional area.   Responsibilities: This clinical position requires teaching and service. Collaborate with school administrators. Collaborate with the Department of Educator & Leadership Preparation. Other service and committee work at the program, department, college, university, community, and profession levels. Ensure alignment of program operations to the work of the department and college. Assess, evaluate, and recommend opportunities for collaboration with partners. Support broader department initiatives during the academic year. Coordinate program initiatives, ensuring unity of focus and purpose. Required Education & Experience: Successful candidates will have an earned doctoral degree from an accredited institution of higher education in the field of Educational Leadership or a closely related discipline. The successful candidate will have vast experience chairing dissertations. The successful candidate will have demonstrated record of successfully mentoring doctoral candidates through degree completion. A successful academic record that meets the University and A&M system qualifications for tenure. Preferred Education & Experience: Experience working with both quantitative and qualitative dissertations. Experience working with Local Education Agencies and Institutions of Higher Education. Administrative experience at the University level. Superintendent Certification and experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others. Strong self-discipline and ability to work independently. Ability to communicate effectively with faculty and students. Ability to interact with students from multicultural backgrounds. Ability to develop capacity in teachers and education leaders to work successfully with students of varied experiences and backgrounds. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with employees, community groups, educators, parents, civic associations and the general public as necessitated by the work. Knowledge of the design and development of curriculum to support teaching and service. Skill in utilizing computer software. Ability to prepare and maintain required reports and records. Develop visual aids and other instructional materials to meet specific training need. Review of applications will begin one week after posting and will continue until the position is filled. Finalists will be required to facilitate the submission of three original letters of recommendation to the Search Committee Chair to the address provided. The letters should be less than one year old and should bear the writer's actual signature.   Prior to issuing a letter of appointment, official transcripts must be received directly from each degree-granting institution by the Office of the Dean, Texas A&M University-San Antonio, College of Education & Human Development, One University Way, San Antonio, Texas 78224. We cannot accept transcripts issued directly to the candidate. If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator.   For questions, please contact the following: Associate /Full Professor-Educational Leadership c/o Dr. Esther Garza (e-mail egarza@tamusa.edu) Texas A&M University-San Antonio College of Education and Human Development One University Way San Antonio, TX 78224 Applicant   Instructions:     Please make sure to provide the following documents:    Cover Letter   Resume   / CV   Professional References   For detailed instructions on how to apply for any position on our website, please use the following link:    http://www.tamusa.edu/humanresources/job-opportunities/index.html   ​     Summary of Employee Benefits:     www.tamusa.edu/human-resources/documents/Summary-of-Employees-Benefits1.pdf     Texas A&M University-San Antonio values community engagement and encourages applicants who are committed to advancing the well-being and prosperity of our communities.    Please ensure that all required documents are uploaded prior to   submitting   the application. Once   the   application is   submitted , no changes or revisions can be made.  If you have issues with adding documents   to   your application, please contact HR at 210-784-2058.     In compliance with ADA, if accommodations are needed for the application process, please contact HR at (210) 784-2058.    A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025.   Please be advised that Texas   A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to   ascertain   whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee.   In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission.   Accordingly , if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status, this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUSA_External/job/San-Antonio-TX/Associate-Professor-in-Educational-Leadership--Research-Methodology-_R-091544": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Educational Leadership (Research Methodology)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-05\nFull time\n\nJob Title Associate Professor in Educational Leadership (Research Methodology) Agency Texas A&M University - San Antonio Department Department Of Educator & Leadership Preparation Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location San Antonio, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Texas A&M University – San Antonio (TAMU-SA) seeks a dynamic leader for the position of Associate Professor in Educational Leadership (Research Methodology). This is a full-time tenure-track position. This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Educator and Leadership Preparation. Texas A&M University – San Antonio is a Hispanic-serving, upper-division and graduate institution. The University has enjoyed tremendous growth in enrollment since it became a stand-alone University in 2009.  Enrollment is estimated to have been nearly 8,000 students in 2025. The University offers a variety of undergraduate, graduate and certificate programs. Instruction may be delivered on-campus, off-campus, or online and may be during the day and/or evening. Responsibilities: Teach courses within the required discipline each semester at both the graduate and post-graduate levels. Assist doctoral students in designing and refining statistical analysis and methodologies used in social science research and for dissertations. Serve on dissertation committees. Develop and manage the class syllabi and ensure that the syllabi meet department and college standards. Plan and create lectures, in class discussions, and assignments. Assess grades for students based on participation, performance in class, assignments, and examinations. Assist/mentor students as needed. Other duties as assigned. Required Education and Experience: Successful candidates will have an earned doctoral degree from an accredited institution of higher education in the field of Measurement/Evaluation/Research Methods/Educational Psychology/School Psychology/Organizational Behavior or a closely related field. The successful candidate will have demonstrated record of teaching measurement/evaluation courses at the doctoral level with an emphasis on statistical analysis. The successful candidate will have demonstrated record of publications utilizing quantitative methodologies. The successful candidate will have demonstrated record of serving on dissertation committees for doctoral candidates utilizing quantitative methodologies. Preferred Education and Experience: Demonstrated record of successfully mentoring doctoral candidates through degree completion. Demonstrated record of publications utilizing the following methodologies: Structural Equation Modeling; Hierarchical Linear Modeling; and/or Linear Regression Modeling. Administrative experience in K-12 education. Superintendent Certification and experience. Applicant   Instructions:     Please make sure to provide the following documents:    Cover letter Resume/CV Transcripts (unofficial will be accepted with application. Official transcripts are required upon acceptance of verbal offer). For detailed instructions on how to apply for any position on our website, please use the following link:    http://www.tamusa.edu/humanresources/job-opportunities/index.html   ​     Summary of Employee Benefits:     www.tamusa.edu/human-resources/documents/Summary-of-Employees-Benefits1.pdf     Texas A&M University-San Antonio values community engagement and encourages applicants who are committed to advancing the well-being and prosperity of our communities.    Please ensure that all required documents are uploaded prior to   submitting   the application. Once   the   application is   submitted , no changes or revisions can be made.  If you have issues with adding documents   to   your application, please contact HR at 210-784-2058.     In compliance with ADA, if accommodations are needed for the application process, please contact HR at (210) 784-2058.    A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025.   Please be advised that Texas   A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to   ascertain   whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee.   I n addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission.   Accordingly , if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status, this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/TAMUSA_External/job/San-Antonio-TX/Adjunct-Faculty---Psychology_R-098392-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nPart time\n\nJob Title Adjunct Faculty - Psychology Agency Texas A&M University - San Antonio Department Department of Health and Behavioral Sciences Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location San Antonio, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description The Department of Health and Behavioral Sciences is seeking to hire a part-time adjunct faculty of Psychology at Texas A&M University—San Antonio. This is an adjunct position, requiring only teaching. Courses could be offered days, evenings, or weekends, based on departmental need.  Most courses needed are offered in person. Required Education and Experience: Masters degree in Psychology from an accredited university. Teaching experience. Broad training in psychology. Preferred Education and Experience: Doctoral degree in Psychology from an accredited university. Experience serving as an instructor of record at the college/university level. Experience teaching at a multicultural university. Experience teaching in a non-traditional commuter university setting. Ability to teach a range of courses in psychology. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to work cooperatively with others. Strong self-discipline and ability to work independently. Ability to communicate effectively with faculty, staff, and students. Ability to interact with students from multicultural backgrounds. Finalists will be required to provide three current, original letters of recommendation to the Search Committee Chair via email (sent directly from the recommender), or at the address listed below. The letters should be less than one year old and should bear the writer's actual signature. Prior to issuing a letter of appointment, official transcripts must be received directly from each degree-granting institution by the Office of Academic Affairs, TAMU-SA, One University Way, San Antonio, TX 78224. We cannot accept transcripts issued directly to the candidate. If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcript translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator. For questions, please contact Dr. Alan Daniel, adaniel@tamusa.edu Letters of recommendation for finalists may be sent to: Adjunct Instructor of Psychology c/o Jessica McDonald (email: jgillenwate@tamusa.edu) Texas A&M University-San Antonio Department of Health and Behavioral Sciences One University Way San Antonio, TX 78224 Selected candidates must pass a pre-employment background investigation to be hired for this position. Applicant Instructions:    Please make sure to provide the following documents:   Cover Letter  Resume / CV   Professional References    For detailed instructions on how to apply for any position on our website, please use the following link:   http://www.tamusa.edu/humanresources/job-opportunities/index.html ​      Summary of Employee Benefits:    www.tamusa.edu/human-resources/documents/Summary-of-Employees-Benefits1.pdf      Texas A&M University-San Antonio values community engagement and encourages applicants who are committed to advancing the well-being and prosperity of our communities.     Please ensure that all required documents are uploaded prior to submitting the application. Once the application is submitted, no changes or revisions can be made.  If you have issues with adding documents to your application, please contact HR at 210-784-2058.      In compliance with ADA, if accommodations are needed for the application process, please contact HR at (210) 784-2058. A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee. In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status, this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    }
